{"$schema":"https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"artifacts":[{"contents":{"text":"<scxml xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml\" version=\"1.0\" initial=\"red\">\n  <state id=\"red\">\n    <onentry>\n      <send event=\"timer.green\" delay=\"3s\" sendid=\"send_timer_green\"/>\n    </onentry>\n    <transition event=\"timer.green\" target=\"green\"/>\n  </state>\n  <final id=\"green\"/>\n</scxml>\n"},"location":{"uri":"tests/ui/xsd-send-sendid-counterpart.scx"},"mimeType":"application/scxml+xml"}],"columnKind":"utf16CodeUnits","properties":{"diagnosticCounts":{"errors":1,"notes":0,"total":1,"warnings":0},"producer":{"kind":"validator"}},"results":[{"fixes":[{"artifactChanges":[{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/xsd-send-sendid-counterpart.scx"},"replacements":[{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":6,"byteOffset":152,"endColumn":50,"endLine":4,"startColumn":44,"startLine":4},"insertedContent":{"text":"id"}}]}],"description":{"text":"rename `sendid` to `id`"},"properties":{"applicability":"machine-applicable"}}],"level":"error","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/xsd-send-sendid-counterpart.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":50,"endLine":4,"startColumn":44,"startLine":4}}}],"message":{"markdown":"attribute `sendid` is not allowed on `<send>`\n\n**Note:** the W3C SCXML 1.0 schema rejects this under XML Schema constraint `cvc-complex-type.3.2.2`: Attribute 'sendid' is not allowed for this element\n\n**Help:** did you mean `id`? a `<send>` declares its ID with `id`; `sendid` is how `<cancel>` refers to that ID\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §6.2 <send>\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §6.3 <cancel>\n\n**Spec:** XML Schema 1.0 Part 1 §3.4.4 Element Locally Valid (Complex Type) (`cvc-complex-type.3.2.2`)","text":"attribute `sendid` is not allowed on `<send>`"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":158,"start":152},"category":"schema"},"ruleId":"XSD-cvc-complex-type.3.2.2"}],"tool":{"driver":{"informationUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/","name":"scxml-validator","rules":[{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"SCXML elements accept only their declared attributes; extension attributes must be namespace-qualified"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: correct the attribute name (an attribute of a related element becomes this element's own, such as `id` for `<cancel>`'s `sendid` on `<send>`), remove it, or qualify an extension attribute with a namespace prefix.\n\nSpecification: XML Schema 1.0 Part 1 §3.4.4 Element Locally Valid (Complex Type)\n\nRun `scx --explain XSD-cvc-complex-type.3.2.2` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-1/#cvc-complex-type","id":"XSD-cvc-complex-type.3.2.2","name":"XSD-cvc-complex-type.3.2.2","properties":{"category":"schema"},"shortDescription":{"text":"an attribute is not declared for this element"}}],"semanticVersion":"0.2.0"}}}],"version":"2.1.0"}